Cloud Ops 3D

The island, robot, task crates, execution lanes, action pads, ant and reward motifs,
and procedural music were adapted from the user's teammate's contribution:
"Cloud Ops 3D: Jadilah Scheduler", supplied as dunia3d (1).html.
No individual author name was supplied. Credit remains with the teammate and
Kelompok 8 SOKA. The original supplied file is retained locally in the ignored
work/cloud-ops-before/original.html backup; it is not used as runtime code.

The integrated controller and 3D adapter consume the existing scheduling engine.
Original scripted schedules, comparison tables and optimization claims were
replaced with calculated mappings, metrics and actual event traces.

